 weight loss (fitness preparation)"], "excluded_candidates": ["Acute Cholecystitis: less likely given diffuse pattern but included as differential", "Ectopic Pregnancy: possible but reduced by contraceptive use", "Eating Disorder Complications: chronic weight loss history but acute presentation suggests acute abdomen", "Alcohol-Induced Hepatitis: possible but hypotension/shock patterns suggest more critical processes", "Medication-Induced GI Bleeding: ibuprofen use is a risk factor but would require further evidence"], "alarm_features": ["Hypotension (80/40 mmHg) with tachycardia (110 bpm)", "Fever (37.5°C)", "Recent unprotected sexual activity", "Rapid weight loss (10/10 pain pattern suggests acute process)", "Acute haemodynamic instability"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Obstetric/Gynecologic Emergency", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.15644496253606707, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Localized RUQ pain is non-specific for biliary obstruction but provides moderate evidence for gynecological emergencies and visceral inflammation. Exercise-ind…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3", "B1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Acute Visceral Inflammation", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.16178389494544737, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Localized RUQ pain is non-specific for biliary obstruction but provides moderate evidence for gynecological emergencies and visceral inflammation. Exercise-ind…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.